[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2645380695","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102574#issuecomment-2645380695","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102574","id":2645380695,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6drU5X","user":{"login":"haslingerm","id":1212708,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTI3MDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1212708?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/haslingerm","html_url":"https://github.com/haslingerm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haslingerm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haslingerm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haslingerm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haslingerm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haslingerm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haslingerm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haslingerm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haslingerm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haslingerm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-08T12:37:57Z","updated_at":"2025-02-08T12:39:12Z","body":"I have the same issue and tried a couple of things which lead me to speculate that it seems to affect all X11 (via XWayland) windows:\n \n- When I use 'prefer wayland' in the editor then the editor window itself remains operable and has the mouse cursor while in a breakpoint\n  - Other windows (like e.g. dolphin or a Konsole) also remain normally operable\n  - The mouse also appears over the panel while captured and in the brekpoint\n- But all windows running X11 via XWayland don't have a mouse cursor - it disappears the moment I move it over them and reappears when it moves back over a Wayland window\n  - Rider (and other JB IDEs) still rely on XWayland right now, [with Wayland support underway but not ready](https://blog.jetbrains.com/platform/2024/07/wayland-support-preview-in-2024-2/)\n    - *Applying the experimental VM option and running Rider under Wayland seems to solve the issue for me* => might be a workaround for the time being **if** Wayland is used, I don't have a solution for X11, so this won't help everyone\n  - I have Proton Mail which also uses XWayland for the desktop client (actually just a wrapper of the website), but the cursor issue while captured is the same there as well\n\nSystem: Fedora KDE (6.12.11-200.fc41.x86_64) - Wayland - v4.4.beta3.mono.official.06acfccf8","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2645380695/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2691009047","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102574#issuecomment-2691009047","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102574","id":2691009047,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gZYoX","user":{"login":"ToastedOven","id":49164897,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5MTY0ODk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49164897?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ToastedOven","html_url":"https://github.com/ToastedOven","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ToastedOven/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ToastedOven/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ToastedOven/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ToastedOven/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ToastedOven/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ToastedOven/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ToastedOven/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ToastedOven/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ToastedOven/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-28T15:58:54Z","updated_at":"2025-02-28T16:00:08Z","body":"Just chiming in with another potential solution since I found Rider in Wayland mode is quite annoying to use right now (mainly randomly floating text boxes)\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e516fdbf-92d2-4835-938d-bf1abcdbb4a8)\nAdding `--display-driver wayland` to your program arguments will run your Godot project in Wayland mode while letting Rider stay in XWayland mode","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2691009047/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2693562084","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102574#issuecomment-2693562084","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102574","id":2693562084,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gjH7k","user":{"login":"TibAverus","id":71099717,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMDk5NzE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71099717?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TibAverus","html_url":"https://github.com/TibAverus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TibAverus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TibAverus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TibAverus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TibAverus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TibAverus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TibAverus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TibAverus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TibAverus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TibAverus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-03T08:03:57Z","updated_at":"2025-03-03T08:03:57Z","body":"That's unfortunately not a solution for a system that uses X11 only, as Godot will just throw some errors that it cannot initialize wayland and will just use fallback X11 things, but thank you for the tip!","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2693562084/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2870008934","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102574#issuecomment-2870008934","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102574","id":2870008934,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rENxm","user":{"login":"dreams-of-nothing","id":46723863,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NzIzODYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46723863?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dreams-of-nothing","html_url":"https://github.com/dreams-of-nothing","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dreams-of-nothing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dreams-of-nothing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dreams-of-nothing/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dreams-of-nothing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dreams-of-nothing/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dreams-of-nothing/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dreams-of-nothing/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dreams-of-nothing/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dreams-of-nothing/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-11T17:11:11Z","updated_at":"2025-05-11T17:11:11Z","body":"Getting the same problem on:\n\nGodot ver.: v4.4.1.stable.mono.official [49a5bc7b6]\nIDE Used: JetBrains Rider 2025.1\nOS: Arch Linux x86_64\nKernel: 6.14.5-arch1-1\nWindow Manager: XFWM4\nDesktop Environment: Xfce 4.20\n\nI'm also using X11 and can't use wayland display driver","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2870008934/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2927416769","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102574#issuecomment-2927416769","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102574","id":2927416769,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ufNXB","user":{"login":"roopekt","id":98045548,"node_id":"U_kgDOBdgObA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98045548?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roopekt","html_url":"https://github.com/roopekt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roopekt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roopekt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roopekt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roopekt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roopekt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roopekt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roopekt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roopekt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roopekt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-01T15:23:02Z","updated_at":"2025-06-01T15:23:02Z","body":"For X11 users: Minimizing the game window worked for me. On Plasma this can be done with Alt+Tab to switch to the game, and then Meta+PageDown. [Sending the XF86Ungrab key](https://unix.stackexchange.com/questions/40458/command-for-forcing-a-pointer-ungrab-captured-mouse-release) seems to work too, but I haven't tested this.\n\nSystem info:\nGodot: Godot_v4.3-stable_mono_linux.x86_64\nOS: Kubuntu x86_64 (Ubuntu 24.04.2 LTS)\nDE: KDE Plasma 5.27.12\nWM: KWin (X11)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2927416769/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3216931901","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102574#issuecomment-3216931901","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102574","id":3216931901,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6_vnw9","user":{"login":"Polemus","id":112549,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjU0OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112549?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Polemus","html_url":"https://github.com/Polemus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Polemus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Polemus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Polemus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Polemus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Polemus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Polemus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Polemus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Polemus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Polemus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-23T12:48:35Z","updated_at":"2025-08-23T12:54:06Z","body":"Ubuntu x86_64 (Ubuntu 24.04.2 LTS)  \nDE: KDE Plasma 5.27.12  \n\nYes, sending `XF86Ungrab` command does solve the problem.  \n\nI went ahead and created a bash script `force-cursor.sh`, Then make sure it’s executable:\n\n`chmod +x ~/force-cursor.sh`\n\n\nThen just add it to your shortcuts. (for Ubuntu):\n\nOpen Settings → Keyboard → Custom Shortcuts.\n\nhere is the script\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\n# Enable grab-breaking if not already active\nsetxkbmap -option grab:break_actions\n# Force ungrab via xdotool\nxdotool key XF86Ungrab\n# Refresh cursor image\nxsetroot -cursor_name left_ptr\nxdotool mousemove_relative 0 0```\n\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3216931901/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":4,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]